[.BLOCK_LANG_EN]
==== 12.5 Electronic program guides

____
[.BLOCK_LANG_EN]
--
Where ICT displays an Electronic Programme Guide (EPG) presenting media item(s), and information is available
about the availability of subtitles, audio description, spoken subtitles, or sign language interpretation for the media
item(s),
the ICT shall provide a mode of operation in which the availability of subtitles, audio description, spoken subtitles, sign
language can be determined without activating the media item(s).

NOTE 1: 
The information about which accessibility features are available is needed when users are assessing which
programs will be accessible to them. They will need this information to be available to them when they
are viewing or scrolling through the EPG.

NOTE 2: 
Best practice is to display information about all accessibility features as they are developed.
--
